{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/616293-smelling-the-prey","id":616293,"title":"smelling the prey","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-05T04:52:11-07:00","id":616293,"title":"smelling the prey","content":"I have a doubt. In a cronichle I'm mastering a wolves pack were hunting a PC in a forest. She was riding a horse and after a altitude difference of the terrain she was hidden from the sight for a short time and she decided to jump down from the horse and hide im the vegetation while the horse still run away. <br /> The question is: how deal an appropriate dice roll to see if the wolves (or any other creature) smell the PC even if they were running trought the horse fallow him ti view??? I mean: if the wolves are actively try to smell a prey I should make the appropriate roll with some penality if the pc try to hide her smell with mud or sonething else. But if the wokves are chasing the horse at full speed using their sight the dice pool for the smelling roll can't be the same right???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T05:08:28-07:00","id":616325,"title":"","content":"Right. Maybe a dice roll isn't even needed here? Seems like only a small chance they'd smell her. I'd probably apply like a -5 penalty for distraction and other focuses if there was a roll at all. However, if you want this to be a tense moment, you could do other things. Have the pack rush by, not noticing her, but then one of them lags behind. He's going slower, limping from tripping earlier. He stops close to her hiding place and sniffs the air. He gets a normal roll. Now you can have one of those movie moments where he gets close to her hiding spot and then breaks off at the last moment as his pack calls him (if he failed the roll), or he could find her, but now at least she only has to deal with 1 wolf, which she may be able to do in a fight.<br /> <br /> Would be a cool narrative way to reward the player for being smart with the horse (most of the pack moves on automatically) while still keeping the tension up.<br /> <br /> Also, did you mean to post this in the vampire section? There's a general world of darkness section too. I'm sure some moderator can move it if it was a mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T05:13:54-07:00","id":616330,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear, are we talking regular wolves or the were- sort?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T05:34:30-07:00","id":616349,"title":"","content":"@Unahim:<br /> Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> @ Elfive:<br /> In this case regular wolves but what kind of difference with were-sort?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T05:49:31-07:00","id":616362,"title":"","content":"Well, a werewolf would probably be more likely to notice the horse had lost its rider. Also they have magic that can aid tracking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 08-05-2015, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T06:02:35-07:00","id":616374,"title":"","content":"Oh ok I understand. Can you suggest me the appropriate roll to make in all these case? For example what roll would be appropriate to see in the night if a far black horse have still his rider?<br /> And to try to find an hidden PC using smell and hearing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T06:13:01-07:00","id":616376,"title":"","content":"I think it depends on what the rider was wearing. Wolves have pretty good night vision, but if they're in dark clothes that'd probably be pushing it. A regular wolf would just focus on the big smelly horse and so wouldn't think to actually check so we're talking a basic wits + composure roll. <br /> <br /> Vampires have a bit of an advantage as far as tracking by smell goes. They don't sweat or anything, so generally they're harder to smell than a human would be. A horse might drown it out completely. So, yeah, against regular wolves I think your player's trick is likely to go off without a hitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T10:16:04-07:00","id":616652,"title":"","content":"Wolves don't track by sight, and yes they will notice that the rider and horse have separated. If your PC can't find a way to break a scent trail, possibly by passing through a stream or river, then the wolves will find them. Quite easily too, if the PC should happen to be bleeding from cuts and scratches they got from riding blindly through foliage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T10:21:55-07:00","id":616656,"title":"","content":"I was assuming the PC was a vamp, what with the forum this was posted in. They don't bleed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T10:28:43-07:00","id":616660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/616293-smelling-the-prey?p=616656#post616656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was assuming the PC was a vamp, what with the forum this was posted in. They don't bleed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think they can, if they have Blush of Life active.<br /> <br /> As for the dice roll, a perception check with some bonuses for actively searching and some penalties for the distractions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-05-2015, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T16:54:34-07:00","id":618217,"title":"","content":"If the PC is a vamp, regular wolves aren't likely to follow him to begin with. He smells funny, while they can go for a succulent horse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}